abstract: >-
  Open-source Apache-2.0 research, simulation, and software-verification testbed
  for a 240 kg coaxial X8 urban eVTOL (VertiRTA-X8-240) and 8+1 Lift+Cruise
  transition platform along the Istanbul Maltepe-Dragos-Kartal coastal corridor
  bounded by real DHMI AIP LTFJ/LTBX control zones. Combines a freestanding
  zero-heap 400 Hz ARM Cortex-M7 C++17 flight core (28,886 B Flash, 0 B static
  RAM, 2,960 B stack DAG), a 100 Hz GPU-solved 4D HJI-CBVF-QP safety filter,
  live ESBMC v8.7.0 supplemental formal proofs (1,905/1,905 properties), live
  Renode dual-FCC OpenCyphal CAN-FD SIL (12.50 ms failover), a <150 KiB
  single-threaded WebAssembly VertiGCS console, a nanobind Python/Gymnasium SDK,
  20-eVTOL U-Space + Part-IS (EU) 2023/203 security, and isolated advisory
  bilingual Z3 Co-Pilot and zero-ShareAlike visual SLZ stacks.
